    "label": "thm:mle_lower_bound",
    "number": "Theorem 3",
    "quote": "Let $\\delta \\in (0,1/8)$. Fix $\\X, \\Z \\subset \\R^d$ and $\\Theta = \\R^d$. Fix a problem $\\theta \\in \\Theta$. Then, if the non-interactive MLE is $\\delta$-PAC wrt $(\\X, \\Z, \\Theta)$ where a different allocation can be used for each $\\theta \\in \\Theta$, then it uses at least $c( \\gamma^*+\\rho^{\\ast}\\log(1/\\delta))$ samples for the instance $(\\X, \\Z, \\theta)$ where $c > 0$ is a universal constant."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Lower bound only for the non-interactive oracle MLE procedure (fixed allocation chosen with knowledge of theta), not for adaptive algorithms. Number of samples is deterministic."
  },
